@feat:FEAT-POC-007-demo-data-reset @demo-reset
Feature: Demo Data Reset
  As a donor exploring the platform during a demo
  I want to reset my own demo data to a clean slate from my account menu
  So that the next demo starts fresh without touching anyone else's data or the platform's production safeguards

  Background:
    Given the platform hosts several donors, their attorneys, and an administrator

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # GROUP A: Key Examples
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: The headline path — a demo-mode donor wipes their whole footprint in one action and returns to a clean login
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-007 — the wipe also clears the donor's rules-application and voice-narration jobs
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: A donor in demo mode resets their demo data to a clean slate
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with an uploaded LPA, connected bank data, and flagged transactions
    When I reset my demo data
    Then my LPA, extracted rules, bank connections, accounts, transactions and flags should all be removed
    And I should be signed out
    And when I sign in again my dashboard should be empty

  # Why: Flags are reachable only through the bank chain (no direct donor link); the wipe must still remove every one
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Resetting removes all of the donor's flagged transactions
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor who has flagged transactions
    When I reset my demo data
    Then none of my flagged transactions should remain

  # Why: The reset clears the LPA record, its extracted rules, and the uploaded PDF file on the storage volume
  @key-example
  Scenario: Resetting clears the donor's LPA, its extracted rules, and the uploaded document
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor who has a confirmed LPA with extracted rules
    When I reset my demo data
    Then my LPA and its extracted rules should be removed
    And the uploaded LPA document should be deleted from storage

  # Why: Only the donor's link to each attorney is removed; attorney accounts are shared across donors and must survive
  @key-example
  Scenario: Resetting removes the donor's attorney relationships but keeps the attorney accounts
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor who has active attorney relationships
    When I reset my demo data
    Then my attorney relationships should be removed
    And each of those attorneys should still be able to sign in

  # Why: A single "demo data reset" record is kept as evidence the action happened, written after the donor's audit purge
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-006 — the audit purge is scoped to the donor's own context, leaving request-log rows keyed only by user id
  @key-example
  Scenario: A record of the reset is kept after the donor's audit history is purged
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with existing audit history
    When I reset my demo data
    Then my earlier audit history should be purged
    And a record that my demo data was reset should remain

  # Why: The reset option appears on the donor's own account menu, and only in demo mode
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-004 — the menu option is labelled "Reset demo data"
  @key-example
  Scenario: A donor in demo mode sees a reset option on their account menu
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor
    When I open my account menu
    Then it should offer a "Reset demo data" option

  # Why: The action is irreversible, so it asks for explicit confirmation and only wipes after the donor confirms
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] ASSUM-005 — confirmation is a simple confirm dialog, not a type-to-confirm challenge
  @key-example
  Scenario: Choosing reset asks for confirmation before wiping
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor
    When I choose "Reset demo data" from my account menu
    Then I should be asked to confirm that this permanently wipes my demo data
    And no data should be removed until I confirm

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # GROUP B: Boundary Conditions
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: Empty-footprint boundary — a donor who has uploaded nothing can still reset without error
  @boundary
  Scenario: Resetting a donor who has no data succeeds and leaves an empty dashboard
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a newly onboarded donor with no LPA and no bank connection
    When I reset my demo data
    Then the reset should succeed
    And when I sign in again my dashboard should be empty

  # Why: Connection-status boundary — only active connections are revoked at the provider; revoked or pending ones are not
  # operator_handoff: the real provider revoke can only be proven against the live Moneyhub sandbox (see TASK-MH03-009)
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-002 — provider revocation defaults to enabled
  @boundary @operator-handoff
  Scenario: Only active bank connections are revoked at the provider
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with one active, one already-revoked, and one pending bank connection
    When I reset my demo data with provider revocation enabled
    Then bank consent should be cancelled at the provider only for the active connection
    And all of my bank connections should be removed locally

  # Why: Toggle boundary — with provider revocation disabled, no provider call is made and only local data is cleared
  @boundary
  Scenario: With provider revocation disabled no bank consent is cancelled at the provider
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with an active bank connection
    When I reset my demo data with provider revocation disabled
    Then no bank consent should be cancelled at the provider
    And my local bank data should still be removed

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # GROUP C: Negative Cases
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: Production-safety gate — outside demo mode the reset must be invisible, as if the feature does not exist
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-001 — demo mode defaults to off; ASSUM-009 — the reset responds as not-found when demo mode is off
  @negative @smoke
  Scenario: The reset is unavailable when demo mode is disabled
    Given demo mode is disabled
    And I am signed in as a donor
    When I attempt to reset my demo data
    Then the platform should behave as if the reset feature does not exist
    And none of my data should be removed

  # Why: The donor reset targets the caller's own footprint; an attorney has none, so the action is refused for them
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] ASSUM-003 — a non-donor caller is refused, not silently accepted as a no-op
  @negative
  Scenario: An attorney cannot use the donor demo reset
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as an attorney
    When I attempt to reset donor demo data
    Then the reset should be refused

  # Why: The reset is self-service and requires a signed-in donor; an anonymous request is rejected
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] ASSUM-008 — an unauthenticated request is rejected as unauthorised
  @negative
  Scenario: An unauthenticated request cannot reset demo data
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am not signed in
    When I attempt to reset demo data
    Then the request should be rejected as unauthorised

  # Why: The option is hidden for anyone who should not see it — outside demo mode, or a non-donor role
  @negative
  Scenario Outline: The reset option is hidden when it should not be shown
    Given I am signed in as <role>
    And demo mode is <mode>
    When I open my account menu
    Then it should not offer a "Reset demo data" option

    Examples:
      | role        | mode     |
      | a donor     | disabled |
      | an attorney | enabled  |

  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # GROUP D: Edge Cases
  # ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  # Why: Scoping guarantee — one donor's reset must never touch another donor's data
  @edge-case @smoke
  Scenario: Resetting one donor leaves another donor's data untouched
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And another donor has an LPA, bank data, and flagged transactions
    And I am signed in as a donor with my own data
    When I reset my demo data
    Then the other donor's LPA, bank data and flagged transactions should be unchanged

  # Why: Identities are preserved — the donor, every attorney, and the administrator can still sign in after a reset
  @edge-case
  Scenario: All user identities survive a reset
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with attorney relationships
    When I reset my demo data
    Then I should still be able to sign in afterwards
    And every attorney and the administrator should still be able to sign in

  # Why: Failure recovery — a provider revoke error must be tolerated and logged, never aborting the local wipe
  # operator_handoff: forcing a provider revoke error is proven against the live Moneyhub sandbox
  @edge-case @operator-handoff
  Scenario: A provider revocation failure does not prevent the local data wipe
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with an active bank connection
    And the provider will reject the revocation request
    When I reset my demo data with provider revocation enabled
    Then my local LPA, bank data and flagged transactions should still be removed
    And I should be signed out

  # Why: After a reset the attorney's delegated access to that donor ends; their next request for that donor is refused
  @edge-case
  Scenario: An attorney loses delegated access to a donor after that donor resets
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And an attorney has active delegated access to my donor account
    And I am signed in as that donor
    When I reset my demo data
    Then the attorney should no longer have delegated access to my account

  # Why: Defence against flag drift — if the platform reports the feature unavailable, the menu option hides regardless of build flags
  @edge-case
  Scenario: The reset option disappears when the platform reports the feature unavailable
    Given the app was built with the demo reset option enabled
    But the platform has demo mode disabled
    When I open my account menu as a donor
    Then the "Reset demo data" option should not remain available

  # Why: Self-scoping security — the reset acts only on the authenticated donor and ignores any donor identifier in the request
  @edge-case @negative
  Scenario: The reset only ever affects the authenticated donor
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And another donor has an LPA, bank data, and flagged transactions
    And I am signed in as a donor
    When I reset my demo data and attempt to name the other donor as the target
    Then only my own data should be removed
    And the other donor's data should be unchanged

  # Why: Idempotency — a donor who has already been cleared can reset again without error
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A repeated reset on an already-clean donor is harmless
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor whose demo data has already been reset
    When I reset my demo data again
    Then the reset should succeed
    And my dashboard should remain empty

  # Why: Integration boundary — a missing uploaded document on the volume must not fail the wipe (best-effort delete)
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A missing LPA document on storage does not fail the reset
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor whose uploaded LPA document is already missing from storage
    When I reset my demo data
    Then the reset should succeed
    And my LPA and its extracted rules should be removed

  # Why: Data integrity — the wipe is all-or-nothing; a failure mid-operation must leave the donor's data fully intact
  @edge-case
  Scenario: A failure during the wipe leaves the donor's data fully intact
    Given demo mode is enabled
    And I am signed in as a donor with an uploaded LPA, connected bank data, and flagged transactions
    And the wipe cannot be completed
    When I reset my demo data
    Then none of my LPA, bank data or flagged transactions should be partially removed
